# Copy to .env for local development. Placeholders only — never commit real values.
#
# Secret discipline (docs/architecture/system-overview.md §12): the client bundle is public and
# may hold the client key and nothing else. Every value marked SERVER-ONLY below must never be
# referenced from anything under app/.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Client (app/) — inlined into the public bundle by Vite. Public values only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_TIKTOK_CLIENT_KEY=awxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.invalid

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server (server/) — SERVER-ONLY.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PORT=8080
HOST=0.0.0.0
LOG_LEVEL=info

# SERVER-ONLY. Obtained from the TikTok Developer Portal.
# TIKTOK_CLIENT_SECRET is also the webhook signing key. Without it the payment callback rejects
# every request — that is deliberate, but it means an unset value silently stops entitlement
# delivery, so treat it as a required value in any deployment that takes payments.
TIKTOK_CLIENT_KEY=awxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
TIKTOK_CLIENT_SECRET=replace-me-server-side-only

# Accepted clock skew for a webhook timestamp, in seconds. TikTok's IAP page suggests five minutes.
# Not a switch: no value disables verification, and an unusable value falls back to 300 rather than
# widening the window.
TIKTOK_WEBHOOK_TOLERANCE_SEC=300

# SERVER-ONLY. Mock login. Leave unset.
#
# When set to the exact sentence below *and* NODE_ENV is `test` or `development`, POST /v1/auth/login
# stops talking to TikTok and accepts codes of the form `mock:<userId>`, issuing a real session bound
# to that user id. It exists so the endpoints that need a viewer — progress, favorites, unlocks — are
# testable before the real code exchange lands (server/src/modules/identity/test-login.ts).
#
# It is an authentication bypass. Both conditions are checked, `NODE_ENV` is an allowlist so an unset
# value refuses, and the server logs a warning at every start where the path is live. Do not set this
# in any deployment that anyone but you can reach.
# MINIDRAMA_TEST_LOGIN=yes-i-am-a-non-production-test-deployment

# SERVER-ONLY. Wave 2 datastores.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://minidrama:minidrama@localhost:5432/minidrama
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
